        {"when": "1778 to 1821", "title": "Constantia's golden age", "text": "Hendrik Cloete bought Groot Constantia in 1778 and made an unfortified sweet Muscat wine that became the toast of European courts. Napoleon had it shipped to St Helena during his exile (1815 to 1821); Jane Austen recommended it for a broken heart in Sense and Sensibility (1811), and Baudelaire and Dickens wrote about it.", "lat": -34.0304, "lon": 18.4176},
        {"when": "1834", "title": "Emancipation", "text": "Slavery was abolished in the Cape in 1834 (with a four-year 'apprenticeship'). The 'dop' system of paying farm workers partly in wine, which caused generations of harm, persisted long after and was only outlawed in 1960, though it lingered informally.", "lat": -33.9259, "lon": 18.4267},
