        {"name": "Chenin Blanc", "note": "The most planted variety (about 18 percent of the vineyard). Once brandy and bulk fodder, now made in every style from crisp and fruity to barrel-fermented old-vine wines of great depth, and in sweet and sparkling forms."},
        {"name": "Cabernet Sauvignon", "note": "The leading red grape, especially in Stellenbosch, where Bordeaux blends (Meerlust Rubicon, Kanonkop Paul Sauer, Vergelegen V) are classics."},
